# WorkOS Configuration with RBAC

**Version:** 1.0
**Purpose:** Configure [[WorkOS]] AuthKit for multi-tier role-based access across all panels

## Part 1: WorkOS Organization Structure

### Why Organizations Matter in WorkOS

WorkOS uses "Organizations" to scope users and roles. Each [[MylesCorp Technologies Ltd]] panel type maps to a distinct WorkOS organization pattern so role checks stay clean and auditable.

```
WorkOS Account Structure (per product, e.g., EduMyles)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

1. "EduMyles  -  Platform" (Master Admin org)
   ├─ Members: MylesCorp employees only
   ├─ Role: platform_admin
   └─ Count: ~5-10 users

2. "EduMyles  -  Network [Name]" (one per network)
   ├─ Members: network_operator, operator_manager
   ├─ Roles: network_operator, operator_manager
   └─ Count: 1-3 users per network

3. "EduMyles  -  Agency [Name]" (one per agency)
   ├─ Members: agency staff
   ├─ Role: agency_super_admin (+ agency staff sub-roles)
   └─ Count: varies per agency

4. "EduMyles  -  Reseller [Name]" (one per reseller)
   ├─ Members: reseller staff
   ├─ Role: reseller_super_admin (+ reseller staff sub-roles)
   └─ Count: varies per reseller

5. "EduMyles  -  Partner [Name]" (one per partner integration)
   ├─ Members: partner staff
   ├─ Role: partner_admin, partner_user
   └─ Count: varies per partner

6. "EduMyles  -  Client [School Name]" (one per client organization)
   ├─ Members: client_admin, teacher, student, parent, staff, etc.
   ├─ Roles: product-specific roles
   └─ Count: varies per organization (could be hundreds of users)
```

### Mapping Table: WorkOS Org Type → MylesCorp Entity

| WorkOS Organization Pattern | MylesCorp Table | Created When |
|---|---|---|
| `[Product]  -  Platform` | N/A (singleton) | Once per product at setup |
| `[Product]  -  Network [Name]` | `networks` | When network is onboarded |
| `[Product]  -  Agency [Name]` | `agencies` | When agency is onboarded |
| `[Product]  -  Reseller [Name]` | `resellers` | When reseller is onboarded |
| `[Product]  -  Partner [Name]` | `partners` (or users with partnerId) | When partner integration approved |
| `[Product]  -  Client [Org Name]` | `organizations` | When client is provisioned |

